{"claims":[{"claim_text":"Electoral successes have been paralleled by, and to a large degree made possible by, the rise of a new generation of progressive social movements committed to thoroughgoing critiques of capitalism, racism, sexism, xenophobia and other forms of oppression, as well as to the creation of an ecologically sustainable, democratic and egalitarian future.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"The progressive offensive against neoliberalism in the United States began with the Occupy protests of 2011 and resistance to Governor Scott Walker’s anti-labor offensive in Wisconsin, which put the issue of inequality at the center of U.S. political discourse and cultivated a new generation of activists.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"Powerful new movements arose to challenge brutal immigration policies (The Dreamers), the shamefully low federal minimum wage (Fight for $15), the epidemic of police brutality and structural racism (Black Lives Matter) and inequality (the Sanders Political Revolution).", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"These movements have opened up space for a serious discussion of capitalism, male-dominance and racism in society that has not existed in decades.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"These movements provide unique opportunities for the growth of a democratic socialist movement that emphasizes the interconnectedness of all struggles and the structural character of the reforms needed to make real and lasting change.", "claim_types":["prediction"],"evidence_ids":[1]}],"unresolved_references":[]}
```

